                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Annex]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">Statement of United States Policy Regarding
                        Conversion of Japanese Currency Held by Other Governments and
                    Forces</hi></head>
                <p>It is concluded that:</p>
                <p>The United States is opposed to conversion of yen held by: <list>
                        <label>(1)</label>
                        <item>other governments and forces,</item>
                        <label>(2)</label>
                        <item>Japanese banks for the U.S. Military Government in Korea,</item>
                        <label>(3)</label>
                        <item>private individuals where the currency in question is held outside of
                            Japan.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>The question of conversion of yen of types listed in the above paragraph should
                    be considered in connection with reparations and Japanese external assets.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
